        "original_id": "48793fc5-2704-5ecc-b475-6050f08043a1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Viktor von Weizsäcker, Carl Friedrich von Weizsäcker, Ernst von Weizsäcker, Richard von Weizsäcker, Werner Heisenberg\n- Roles: physician, physiologist, physicist, philosopher\n- Organizations: German nuclear research team in the Second World War\n- Events: Second World War\n\nFacts:\n- Viktor von Weizsäcker was born on 21 April 1886 in Stuttgart and died on 9 January 1957 in Heidelberg.\n- Viktor von Weizsäcker was a German physician and physiologist.\n- Carl Friedrich von Weizsäcker was born on 28 June 1912 and died on 28 April 2007.\n- Carl Friedrich von Weizsäcker was a German physicist and philosopher.\n- Viktor von Weizsäcker was the brother of Ernst von Weizsäcker and the uncle of Richard von Weizsäcker and Carl Friedrich von Weizsäcker.\n- During the Second World War, Carl Friedrich von Weizsäcker was a member of the team that performed nuclear research in Germany under Werner Heisenberg's leadership.\n- Carl Friedrich von Weizsäcker was the longest-living member of Werner Heisenberg's Second World War German nuclear research team.",
